# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase
# Dashboard → Project Settings → API
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGci...

# (Optional) Service role key — only used in server-side admin scripts.
# DO NOT expose this in client code.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google OAuth (for "Sign in with Google")
# Configure inside Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → Providers → Google
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# (No app-side env needed — Supabase handles the OAuth round-trip.)

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Billing (RevenueCat, native only — read in lib/billing/load-native-session.ts)
# Leave NEXT_PUBLIC_BILLING_ENABLED unset/false to skip billing entirely.
#
# With the flag on, the native iOS app shows the Huddle Pro purchase card on
# /membership (components/billing). Web and desktop never show it.
# - These are read when the app is BUILT (`pnpm build:cap`), not when it runs:
#   after changing them, rebuild and `cap sync` before testing.
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY is the PUBLIC SDK key RevenueCat generates
#   for the Apple app (RevenueCat dashboard → API keys). Never put a secret
#   key (those start with "sk_") or any webhook secret here — NEXT_PUBLIC_
#   values ship inside the app.
# - Turn the flag on for sandbox/TestFlight builds only until the server side
#   (docs/billing/launch-checklist.md steps 5-9) is live: a purchase shows as
#   "syncing" and is never treated as Pro until the server confirms it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BILLING_ENABLED=true
# NEXT_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_KEY=
